              "fullDescription": {
                "markdown": "jQuery from 1.1.4 until 3.4.0, as used in Drupal, Backdrop CMS, and other products, mishandles `jQuery.extend(true, {}, ...)` because of `Object.prototype` pollution. If an unsanitized source object contained an enumerable `__proto__` property, it could extend the native `Object.prototype`.",
                "text": "jQuery from 1.1.4 until 3.4.0, as used in Drupal, Backdrop CMS, and other products, mishandles `jQuery.extend(true, {}, ...)` because of `Object.prototype` pollution. If an unsanitized source object contained an enumerable `__proto__` property, it could extend the native `Object.prototype`."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "**Your dependency is vulnerable to [CVE-2019-11358](https://osv.dev/CVE-2019-11358)**\n(Also published as: [PYSEC-2026-628](https://osv.dev/PYSEC-2026-628), [GHSA-6c3j-c64m-qhgq](https://osv.dev/GHSA-6c3j-c64m-qhgq), ).\n\n## [PYSEC-2026-628](https://osv.dev/PYSEC-2026-628)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e jQuery from 1.1.4 until 3.4.0, as used in Drupal, Backdrop CMS, and other products, mishandles `jQuery.extend(true, {}, ...)` because of `Object.prototype` pollution. If an unsanitized source object contained an enumerable `__proto__` property, it could extend the native `Object.prototype`.\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n## [GHSA-6c3j-c64m-qhgq](https://osv.dev/GHSA-6c3j-c64m-qhgq)\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003eDetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n\u003e jQuery from 1.1.4 until 3.4.0, as used in Drupal, Backdrop CMS, and other products, mishandles `jQuery.extend(true, {}, ...)` because of `Object.prototype` pollution. If an unsanitized source object contained an enumerable `__proto__` property, it could extend the native `Object.prototype`.\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n---\n\n### Affected Packages\n\n| Source | Package Name | Package Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| lockfile:/workspace/requirements.txt | django | 2.2.0 |\n\n## Remediation\n\nTo fix these vulnerabilities, update the vulnerabilities past the listed fixed versions below.\n\n### Fixed Versions\n\n| Vulnerability ID | Package Name | Fixed Version |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| GHSA-6c3j-c64m-qhgq | django | 2.1.9, 2.2.2 |\n| GHSA-6c3j-c64m-qhgq | org.webjars.npm:jquery | 3.4.0 |\n| GHSA-6c3j-c64m-qhgq | maximebf/debugbar | 1.19.0 |\n| GHSA-6c3j-c64m-qhgq | jquery | 3.4.0 |\n| GHSA-6c3j-c64m-qhgq | jquery-rails | 4.3.4 |\n| GHSA-6c3j-c64m-qhgq | jQuery | 3.4.0 |\n| PYSEC-2026-628 | django | 2.1.9, 2.2.2 |\n\nIf you believe these vulnerabilities do not affect your code and wish to ignore them, add them to the ignore list in an\n`os